<title>GREECE: Greek drachma mixed vs other currencies in Sept.</title>
<headline>Greek drachma mixed vs other currencies in Sept.</headline>
<dateline>ATHENS 1996-10-03</dateline>
<text>
<p>The drachma was mixed against major currencies in September, firming against the yen and european currencies month-on-month and sliding against the U.S and Canadian dollars, the pound sterling and the Irish punt, Ionian research said in its monthly report.</p>
<p>					 SEPTEMBER</p>
<p>		   (mo/mo pct change)     (yr/yr pct change)</p>
<p> USD=			 1.07		    1.47</p>
<p> ECU=			 0.25		    0.09</p>
<p> DEM=			-0.53		   -1.47</p>
<p> FRF=			-0.27		   -0.21</p>
<p> GBP=			 1.65		    1.63</p>
<p> IEP=			 1.03		    2.82</p>
<p> BEF=			-0.47		   -1.57</p>
<p> NLG=			-0.48		   -1.56</p>
<p> ITL=			 0.79		    7.78</p>
<p> ESP=			 0.07		    0.35</p>
<p> PTE=			 0.00		    0.47</p>
<p> YEN=			-0.78		   -7.28</p>
<p> CHF=			-1.31		   -2.00</p>
<p> CAD=			 1.24		    0.00</p>
<p>All calculations are based on average monthly fixing prices. A minus sign before a currency indicates that the specific foreign currency depreciated against the drachma. --Dimitris Kontogiannis, Athens Newsroom +301 3311812-4</p>
